A starlink satellite dropped 12 kilometers, then climb back, showing how the constellation corrects sudden orbital decay. This is SpaceX Daily, episode 172. Elon Musk has a larger starship in design. Northrop Grumman added falcon cargo for the station. And starshield restrictions are drawing official questions. Then the counterpoint and the engineering deep dive. Starlink 35829, tracked in real time by keep track, used onboard propulsion to answer a burst of atmospheric drag without required

