00:04:06.473 --> 00:04:11.113
The Hall Effect thrusters on that satellite, electric engines that accelerate ionized

00:04:11.113 --> 00:04:16.213
Krypton, from an engineering standpoint, turned a drag spike into a closed loop altitude

00:04:16.213 --> 00:04:18.813
correction using only what was already on board.

00:04:19.453 --> 00:04:25.833
Typical Starlink Altitudes sit near 550 kilometers, where left over atmosphere still exerts measurable

00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:31.533
force and a small density rise from solar activity or orbital position can drop a spacecraft

00:04:31.533 --> 00:04:33.233
several kilometers in days.

00:04:33.913 --> 00:04:37.293
Drag scales with density times velocity squared times area.

00:04:37.833 --> 00:04:41.613
An orbital speed there is roughly 7.6 kilometers per second.

00:04:42.253 --> 00:04:47.293
Earth's gravitational parameter of about 398,600 cubic kilometers

00:04:47.293 --> 00:04:52.273
per second squared, divided by a radius near 6,920 kilometers,

00:04:52.773 --> 00:04:53.693
then square-rooted.

00:04:54.113 --> 00:04:56.653
When the sun heats the thermosphere, density jumps

00:04:56.653 --> 00:04:58.313
while that speed barely changes.

00:04:58.313 --> 00:05:01.913
diseases, so drag rises in proportion and altitude bleeds off.

00:05:02.373 --> 00:05:06.933
A hall effect thruster traps electrons in a magnetic field and uses an electric field

00:05:06.933 --> 00:05:08.153
to accelerate the ions.

00:05:08.873 --> 00:05:14.033
Thrust is tiny next to a chemical engine and specific impulse is high, which fits a slow

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:14.433
climb.

00:05:15.093 --> 00:05:20.193
Each satellite flies a modest crypton load, the propellant gas, meant for staying in slot

00:05:20.193 --> 00:05:21.773
and for dodging conjunctions.

00:05:22.233 --> 00:05:27.633
Recovery depends on those reserves and on thrust to mass, and the correction uses only a fraction

00:05:27.633 --> 00:05:32.593
of the budget. Spread across thousands of satellites, the same trick holds spacing even

00:05:32.593 --> 00:05:38.153
when one spacecraft hits a surprise drag spike. Higher drag at slightly lower altitudes would

00:05:38.153 --> 00:05:43.813
shorten life unless margins or efficiency improve, so the excursion calibrates drag models and

00:05:43.813 --> 00:05:49.193
the minimum impulse that protects constellation geometry. Engineers can compare actual impulse

00:05:49.193 --> 00:05:54.473
against pre-flight predictions to refine solar activity forecasts, which feeds how many extra

00:05:54.473 --> 00:05:56.953
satellites must launch each year to hold coverage.

00:05:57.393 --> 00:06:02.273
Every kilogram of Krypton held back for recoveries is a kilogram not available for ordinary

00:06:02.273 --> 00:06:04.553
station keeping across the design life.

00:06:05.133 --> 00:06:09.833
Isolated incidents fit the current margin, but repeated events at solar maximum would

00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:10.313
accumulate.

00:06:10.993 --> 00:06:16.353
SpaceX can fly a bit higher on average, ring more impulse from each gram, or live with

00:06:16.353 --> 00:06:21.093
slightly shorter satellite lives, and each path prices out differently in how often they

00:06:21.093 --> 00:06:22.233
must launch replacements.

